Z||000000||turbo86se||07-24-2001||11:39 PM||||I'd like to hear any tips or suggestions for cleaning up under the decklid for shows. I've got the Mustang (TOM's) scoop glassed on, so it looks kinda messy underneath. I sanded it down as best as I could and painted it black, which looks decent, but not show-worthy.<P>I'd like to make some kind of cover for the hole, for show only of course. I've seen a mirror, which I like a whole lot, I think it was Rodney's red GT. <P>Anyone have any suggestions and/or pics? Thanks!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||qwikgta||07-25-2001||01:10 PM||||Not sure if this will help, I have seen someone who took a long piece of small vac hose and sliced it down the middle.  Then placed it around the hole to give it a clean edge.  looked like a piece of trim.   It may require some apoxy or something to stay on.  Good luck<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||07-25-2001||03:41 PM||||I'd suggest trying the mirror idea... saw a few cars like that at Dells Run this year.  Someone was selling Stainless steel inserts for $75 a set.  Email me and I'll get you his email address.  As for the rest of the engine compartment/trunk... I don't have a carpet insert currently (damn mice!) so I purchased this vinyl cover from <A HREF="http://ourworld-top.cs.com/fiero4ever1/myhomepage/business.html" TARGET=_blank>http://ourworld-top.cs.com/fiero4ever1/myhomepage/business.html</A><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut1.jpg">  <P><BR>-Rob<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <BR>||||reg||1
